{title: Frames and Bases}
{subtitle: Exodus 6:19; Numbers 3:20–33; 4:29–33; 1 Chronicles 6:19–47; 23:21–23; 24:26–30}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm7] | [Dm] | [Dm7] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The sons of [C]Merari [Dm]are known by name
Mahli and [C]Mushi carry the [F]load
From the [Bb]tribe of [C]Levi’s [Dm]holy line
In [Bb]the wilder[Gm7]ness they stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am7]Frames of the [Dm]tabernacle heavy and [C]strong
Cross[Dm]bars and posts in the dust
Ba[C]ses and pegs [F]and ropes all a[Bb]long
The [C]work of the [Dm]tent they [Gm]must trust
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Car[Am]ry the frames [Dm]and the crossbars [Bb]too
[C]The posts and the [Dm]bases of [Bb]wood
Assigned [C]by name what [F]each man must do
[Bb]For the [C]service of [Dm]the Lord’s house
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Thir[Gm]ty years [Am]old and up [Dm]to fifty
Fit [C]for the [Dm]work of the tent
Under the [C]oversight [F]of Itha[Bb]mar
The [C]priest’s com[Dm]mand is meant
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Car[Gm]ry the [Am]frames and the crossbars too
The [Bb]posts [C]and the bases [Dm]of wood
As[Bb]signed by name [C]what each man [F]must do
For the [Bb]service [C]of the Lord’s [Dm]house
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Mahli [Gm]and Ed[Am]er and Jer[Dm]emoth
Three sons [C]in the record so [Dm]clear
The clan of Mushi [C]serves with [F]might
Through [Bb]the gen[C]era[Dm]tions near
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Frames and bases [Am]in the [Dm]dust
The Le[C]vites’ faithful [Dm]trust
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
